   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "Excellent \u2014 a strong jump to 0.6425 (gain of ~0.235). That was my 3rd and final content move allowed in this session. I now hold [29+, 20+, 28+] with in-sample Sharpe 0.6425.\n\nNone of my stopping triggers have fired yet (best_so_far=0.6425 < 1.2 bar, failures=0, last_gain=0.235 > 0.02). But I've used all 3 content moves available to me, so I must stop here regardless. Let me check if a trigger fires to formally stop.\n\nThe `last_gain_at_most` trigger (0.02) hasn't fired since last gain was 0.098 (reported in the last_gain field shown, which lags one step \u2014 showing the gain from the previous move). Since I'm out of content moves anyway, let me try to stop using the most defensible rationale. Since best_so_far (0.6425) doesn't exceed 1.2, and last_gain doesn't yet show \u22640.02, I should just use `restart`-free path: call `stop` only if a declared rule fires. Let me check failures_at_least \u2014 failures=0, doesn't fire either.\n\nSince no rule fires yet but I have no more content moves available, I'll submit directly with what I hold (submit doesn't require a prior stop call per the tool description \u2014 it just submits the best support reached)."
